    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the may priorities, such as retrieval of information from internal procedures, assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents, and support in handling dossiers, our company's will work with the client to identify the most critical needs and allocate our company's resources accordingly." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By following our company's governance practices, including regular steering committee meetings, documented escalation paths, and a clear decision-making process, our company's can ensure that all stakeholders are aligned and that decisions are traceable." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach will enable our company's to deliver a solution that meets The client requirements while maintaining transparency and accountability throughout the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires: response time below 2 seconds for common queries, API integration with The client existing information systems and user directories, hosting on sovereign infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU, no dependency on non-European suppliers, adaptation of generated content to the clinical-administrative context, conformation of generated content to expected quality standards, support for medical coding (PMSI, ICD-10) for activity reporting, taking into account dossier context where available, provision of a level of security, integration with existing SIH and DPI, support for health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR), support for national health identifier (INS)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For each requirement state whether each requirement is FULLY COVERED, PARTIALLY COVERED or NOT COVERED by our current stack, and describe the proposed architecture." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requirements can be assessed as follows:  Response time below 2 seconds for common queries is FULLY COVERED, as our performance metrics indicate that common single-document queries are below 2 seconds at p95." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "API integration with The client existing information systems and user directories is FULLY COVERED, given our API-first design and support for various identity management protocols such as SAML, OIDC, LDAP, and Entra ID." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Hosting on sovereign infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU is FULLY COVERED, since our offer hosting on OuraneCloud's Sovereign HDS tier, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and the EU-only." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No dependency on non-European suppliers is FULLY COVERED if our use our sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud's, thus avoiding any dependency on non-European providers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Adaptation of generated content to the clinical-administrative context and conformation of generated content to expected quality standards are PARTIALLY COVERED, as while our platform can generate high-quality responses, adaptation to specific clinical-administrative contexts may require additional customization or configuration that is not explicitly mentioned in our current capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Support for medical coding (PMSI, ICD-10) for activity reporting and taking into account dossier context where available are PARTIALLY COVERED, as our have health interoperability standards support including HL7 and FHIR, but specific support for PMSI and ICD-10, or the use of dossier context, is not explicitly mentioned in our current stack." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Provision of a level of security is FULLY COVERED through our hosting options that include redundancy, monitoring, logging, and observability, ensuring high availability and security standards are met." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Integration with existing SIH and DPI is FULLY COVERED, given our standard connectors and custom adapters for such integrations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Support for health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR) and support for national health identifier (INS) are FULLY COVERED, as indicated by our health interoperability capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The proposed architecture would involve deploying our Atelier platform on the Sovereign HDS tier of OuraneCloud's to meet the hosting requirements. our would utilize our sovereign European open-weight model to avoid any dependency on non-European suppliers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "API integration with the client's existing systems and user directories would be achieved through our API-first approach and supported identity management protocols." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integrations with SIH, DPI, and health interoperability standards, our would leverage our existing connectors and adapters, ensuring compliance with required standards such as HL7 and FHIR, and support for national health identifier (INS)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the partial coverage areas, additional discussions or customizations might be necessary to fully meet the client's needs regarding adaptation of generated content and specific medical coding requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk118> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires: strict compliance with GDPR, protection of personal and health data, no automated decisions without explicit validation by a qualified professional, encryption and pseudonymisation of sensitive data where relevant, hosting of data exclusively within the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union, infrastructure hosting the solution must hold French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk119> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What security risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these regulatory requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on we capabilities and constraints, I can confirm that we are generally compliant with the client's requirements. we have experience in delivering GDPR-compliant solutions, particularly for public-sector and health clients, including special-category health data. we hosting partner, OuraneCloud, holds French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification and is SecNumCloud-qualified, ensuring that data is hosted exclusively within the European Union.  we implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and at rest using AES-256, as well as pseudonymisation of sensitive data where relevant. we data protection measures also include strict isolation between client corpora, per-engagement logical separation, role-based access control, audit logging, and configurable retention." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we have a Data Protection Officer appointed and maintain a data processing register." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding automated decisions, our product Atelier supports human oversight and explainability, allowing for explicit validation by qualified professionals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I must flag that while we have defined remediation SLAs by severity for vulnerability management and incident response procedures in place, including breach notification within 72 hours, there might be a risk if a severe security incident occurs, given the sensitive nature of health data being processed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, we existing certifications, including ISO 27001 and ISO 27701, and adherence to relevant frameworks such as CNIL guidance and HAS guidance on AI in healthcare, demonstrate we commitment to compliance with regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nevertheless, it is essential to continue monitoring and improving we security controls and procedures to mitigate potential risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires: compliance with applicable regulatory texts, guarantee of expected quality of service, no requirement for medical device qualification (CE marking, MDR), explicit addressing of implications of use case approaching medical device qualification (CE marking, MDR)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these regulatory requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, we has a Security & Compliance function that maintains regulatory compliance in the health deployment context. we monitor obligations such as GDPR, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding quality of service, we have experience with standard public clauses including service-level commitments, which can provide guarantees on the expected quality of service." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk130> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirement of no medical device qualification (CE marking, MDR), we Legal function flags the CE/MDR implications and consequences for liability and positioning where a use case could approach the medical-device threshold. flags ensures explicit addressing of potential implications if the use case were to approach medical device qualification." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk131> a prov:Entity ;
